WEBVTT

00:00:00.759 --> 00:00:04.454
Organizational microfoundations—the
cognitions, beliefs,

00:00:04.454 --> 00:00:08.550
and traits of individual members—can
steer firms' strategic decisions,

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.465
operations, and performance.

00:00:11.031 --> 00:00:14.007
These latent cognitive
and psychological properties

00:00:14.007 --> 00:00:16.685
are generally hard
to observe and quantify.

00:00:17.226 --> 00:00:20.534
Behavioral proxies face
the problem of attribution;

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:23.685
narrative proxies face
the problem of authenticity.

00:00:24.228 --> 00:00:26.413
Both face potential measurement errors.

00:00:27.003 --> 00:00:31.062
In this study, we strive to integrate
the behavioral and narrative cues

00:00:31.062 --> 00:00:36.025
for the same latent microfoundational
feature to develop a synthesized proxy.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.633
Step one: Characterizing the Corpus.

00:00:40.175 --> 00:00:42.630
We use unsupervised topic discovery

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:46.722
to establish the thematic structure
emerging from corporate linguistics.

00:00:47.264 --> 00:00:49.804
Step two: Topic decontextualization.

00:00:50.346 --> 00:00:54.189
The task here is one of selection
and interpretation—establishing

00:00:54.189 --> 00:00:57.452
which topics constitute evidence
about the focal feature.

00:00:58.017 --> 00:01:01.113
AI agents first classify
topic descriptors,

00:01:01.113 --> 00:01:04.452
then review common source passages
within their own histories.

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:08.057
An unweighted two-of-three
majority determines selection.

00:01:08.623 --> 00:01:13.028
Agreement measures repeatability,
not independently validated accuracy.

00:01:13.593 --> 00:01:17.188
Step three: Synthesize the narrative
and behavioral proxies.

00:01:17.778 --> 00:01:21.926
Narrative features are used to predict
an established behavioral proxy.

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:25.456
The behavioral outcome,
reconstructed from the narrative

00:01:25.456 --> 00:01:28.610
evidence for observations
excluded from model fitting,

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.972
serves as the synthesized proxy.

00:01:31.513 --> 00:01:35.843
This is the predicted common variation
that the framework seeks to examine.

00:01:36.409 --> 00:01:39.134
Step four: Validate
the synthesized proxy.

00:01:39.676 --> 00:01:41.865
We assess consistency with alternative

00:01:41.865 --> 00:01:45.514
measurements and whether the
synthesized proxy affords extra

00:01:45.514 --> 00:01:49.854
explanatory power beyond the narrative
and behavioral proxies together.

00:01:50.419 --> 00:01:52.421
Evidence of this kind licenses

00:01:52.421 --> 00:01:56.622
a falsifiable proposition rather
than a claim of superiority.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:01.931
To accomplish this task, we
integrate three core AI techniques:

00:02:01.931 --> 00:02:06.246
unsupervised machine learning, AI
agents, and supervised machine learning.

00:02:06.787 --> 00:02:11.460
The aim is a scalable and inspectable
toolkit for organizational research,

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.545
allowing AI judgments
to function as explicit,

00:02:14.545 --> 00:02:17.367
versioned, and falsifiable
measurement inputs.

00:02:17.909 --> 00:02:21.181
The prototype retains judgments
and outputs for inspection.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.988
Comparing alternative topic selections

00:02:23.988 --> 00:02:27.205
through the full analysis
remains a development task.

00:02:28.485 --> 00:02:31.226
We have conducted
a demonstration study to examine

00:02:31.226 --> 00:02:35.881
the feasibility of this workflow,
focusing on CEOs' risk preference.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:41.332
We use CEOs' linguistics in conference
calls to develop narrative features,

00:02:41.332 --> 00:02:44.087
then fit selected topic
densities and overall

00:02:44.087 --> 00:02:48.464
sentiment to research and development
intensity, a behavioral proxy.

00:02:49.005 --> 00:02:50.516
The fitted value is used

00:02:50.516 --> 00:02:54.538
as the synthesized proxy in an
assessment of dividend decisions.

00:02:55.105 --> 00:02:58.757
Higher scores are associated
with lower odds of paying dividends.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.736
The interpretation as underlying CEO

00:03:01.736 --> 00:03:04.984
risk preference still
needs independent evidence.

00:03:06.236 --> 00:03:10.711
The repository provides a connected
prototype and an offline demonstration.

00:03:11.253 --> 00:03:12.763
The empirical review route

00:03:12.763 --> 00:03:16.547
starts from saved text
representations and reader judgments.

00:03:17.137 --> 00:03:20.832
Some reported comparisons remain
outside that reproduction.

00:03:21.399 --> 00:03:24.710
Fresh screening through the newer
API route is not yet ready

00:03:24.710 --> 00:03:26.113
to run from the release.

00:03:26.678 --> 00:03:30.527
A new application needs its own
behavioral and narrative cues,

00:03:30.527 --> 00:03:34.031
validation evidence,
and compatible numerical tools.

00:03:34.573 --> 00:03:37.210
The current adapters
target the CEO case.

00:03:38.444 --> 00:03:41.118
The key assumption is
that this common variation

00:03:41.118 --> 00:03:45.450
is primarily caused by latent
microfoundations as the shared driver.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:48.793
We plan to examine
common-factor variation,

00:03:48.793 --> 00:03:51.909
judgment stability,
and independent human reference.

00:03:52.427 --> 00:03:55.229
If the framework works, it
offers a design template

00:03:55.229 --> 00:03:59.584
that confronts a central empirical
challenge: inherent measurement error,

00:03:59.584 --> 00:04:03.101
helping enhance consistency
between theory and empirics.

